[ a                      owl:Axiom ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy       "https://www.scribbr.com/statistics/interval-data/" ;
  owl:annotatedProperty  rdfs:comment ;
  owl:annotatedSource    om-1:Interval_scale ;
  owl:annotatedTarget    "Interval data is measured along a numerical scale that has equal distances between adjacent values. These distances are called intervals. There is no true zero on an interval scale, which is what distinguishes it from a ratio scale. On an interval scale, zero is an arbitrary point, not a complete absence of the variable."
] .

