oquo-fair-qm:A1_1Characteristic
        a                owl:Class ;
        rdfs:comment     "Degree to which the retrieval protocol is open, free and universally implementable."@en ;
        rdfs:label       "FAIR A1.1 open, free and universally implementable protocol characteristic"@en ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  QualityModel:QualityCharacteristic ;
        obo:IAO_0000115  "Degree to which the communication protocol used to retrieve the resource is open, free of charge and universally implementable, so that anyone can build a client to access it without limitations such as licence fees or undisclosed specifications. Protocols such as HTTP(S) or FTP comply with this subcharacteristic, whereas proprietary or restricted protocols reduce compliance."@en ;
        obo:IAO_0000119  "GO FAIR Foundation, https://www.gofair.foundation/a1-1"@en , "Wilkinson, M. D. et al. (2016). The FAIR Guiding Principles for scientific data management and stewardship. Scientific Data, 3:160018. https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18"@en ;
        dc:source        <https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.18> ;
        rdf1:acronym     "A1.1" .

<https://purl.org/oquo-foops#OntologyPrefixDeclaredMetric>
        a                owl:Class ;
        rdfs:comment     "Whether a preferred prefix for the ontology is declared in its metadata."@en ;
        rdfs:label       "ontology prefix declared metric"@en ;
        rdfs:seeAlso     <https://w3id.org/foops/metric/FIND1> ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  QualityModel:DerivedMeasure ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  [ a                   owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onProperty      QualityModel:hasScale ;
                           owl:someValuesFrom  [ a                   owl:Class ;
                                                 owl:intersectionOf  ( oquo:RawScale
                                                                       [ a               owl:Restriction ;
                                                                         owl:hasValue    QualityModel:HigherBest ;
                                                                         owl:onProperty  QualityModel:hasRankigFunction
                                                                       ]
                                                                     )
                                               ]
                         ] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  [ a                  owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:allValuesFrom  oquo-fair-qm:F3Characteristic ;
                           owl:onProperty     oquo:measuresCharacteristicPositively
                         ] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  [ a               owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:hasValue    <https://purl.org/oquo-foops#OntologyPrefixDeclaredMetricScale> ;
                           owl:onProperty  QualityModel:hasScale
                         ] ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  [ a                   owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onProperty      oquo:measuresCharacteristicPositively ;
                           owl:someValuesFrom  oquo-fair-qm:F3Characteristic
                         ] ;
        obo:IAO_0000115  "This metric checks whether the ontology metadata declare a preferred namespace prefix for the ontology, which helps to refer to the ontology and its namespace unambiguously. The raw value of the metric is the ratio between the number of tests passed and the number of tests run by FOOPS! for this check (total_passed_tests / total_tests_run), so it ranges from 0 to 1 and higher values are better. It measures FAIR principle F3."@en ;
        obo:IAO_0000119  "FOOPS!, https://w3id.org/foops/metric/FIND1"@en ;
        dc:source        <http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2980/paper321.pdf> ;
        rdf1:acronym     "FIND1" .

<http://purl.org/ipo/core#indicatedBy>
        a                 owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:comment      "Indicates a Symptom of this Issue."@en ;
        rdfs:isDefinedBy  <http://purl.org/ipo/core> ;
        rdfs:label        "indicatedBy"@en ;
        owl:inverseOf     <http://purl.org/ipo/core#indicates> .

oquo:hasOutputCardinalValue
        a                owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
        rdfs:comment     "The value of the output cardinal scale onto which the input category of an ordinal to cardinal or nominal to cardinal scale point mapping is converted." ;
        rdfs:domain      [ a            owl:Class ;
                           owl:unionOf  ( oquo:NominalToCardinalScalePointMapping oquo:OrdinalToCardinalScalePointMapping )
                         ] ;
        rdfs:label       "has output cardinal value" ;
        rdfs:range       xsd:double ;
        obo:IAO_0000112  "The value 33.33 in the mapping that converts the category with rank 3 of an ordinal scale whose highest category has rank 9 into a percentage scale." ;
        obo:IAO_0000115  "Relates a scale point mapping whose input is a scale category (an ordinal to cardinal or a nominal to cardinal scale point mapping) with the value of the output cardinal scale onto which the input category of the mapping is converted. Every quality value measured on the input scale that corresponds to the input category of the mapping is converted into this value of the output cardinal scale. The value should fall within the boundaries of the output scale. Each ordinal to cardinal and nominal to cardinal scale point mapping has exactly one output cardinal value." .

